        - Client projects or consulting services
        - Freelance work or professional services
        - Educational institutions charging tuition
        - Non-profit organizations with revenue-generating activities
        - Any entity that generates revenue from any source

1.5 "Derivative Revenue" means any revenue, income, profit, or financial gain 
    that results from, is enabled by, or is in any way connected to the use of 
    the Software, including but not limited to:
    (a) Revenue generated from products or services that incorporate, use, or 
        are based on the Software;
    (b) Revenue generated from activities that are facilitated, improved, or 
        made possible by the Software;
    (c) Cost savings that result in increased profitability;
    (d) Any indirect or consequential financial benefit;
    (e) Revenue from advertising, sponsorships, donations, or other funding 
        sources related to use of the Software;
    (f) Revenue from consulting, training, or support services related to 
        the Software;
    (g) Any other form of economic advantage or financial benefit, whether 
        realized or potential.

1.6 "Personal Use" means use of the Software solely for personal, non-commercial 
    purposes that do not generate any revenue, income, profit, or financial 
    gain, directly or indirectly, and that are not connected to any business, 
    commercial, or profit-making activity.

