================================================================================

3.1 ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION: Commercial Use of the Software is STRICTLY PROHIBITED 
    without a separate, written Commercial License Agreement executed by 
    Licensor. This prohibition applies regardless of:
    (a) Whether the use is direct or indirect;
    (b) Whether the revenue is immediate or future;
    (c) Whether the revenue is realized or potential;
    (d) Whether the use is intentional or unintentional;
    (e) Whether the user is aware that the use constitutes Commercial Use.

3.2 PROHIBITION ON DERIVATIVE REVENUE: Licensee is STRICTLY PROHIBITED from 
    generating, receiving, or benefiting from any Derivative Revenue without 
    a separate, written Commercial License Agreement. This prohibition includes, 
    but is not limited to:
    (a) Revenue from products or services that use, incorporate, or are based 
        on the Software;
    (b) Revenue from activities facilitated by the Software;
    (c) Cost savings that result in increased profitability;
    (d) Advertising revenue, sponsorships, or affiliate income related to 
        use of the Software;
    (e) Consulting, training, or support services related to the Software;
    (f) Any other form of economic benefit, whether direct or indirect.

3.3 PERSONAL USE WITH REVENUE GENERATION: If Licensee's use of the Software, 
    even if initially intended for Personal Use, results in ANY form of revenue, 
    income, profit, or financial gain (including Derivative Revenue), such 
    use IMMEDIATELY becomes Commercial Use and is STRICTLY PROHIBITED. 
    Licensee MUST:
    (a) Immediately cease all use of the Software;
    (b) Immediately notify Licensor in writing;
    (c) Obtain a Commercial License Agreement before any further use;
    (d) Pay all applicable license fees and damages as set forth in this 
        Agreement.

3.4 NO EXCEPTIONS: There are NO exceptions to the prohibition on Commercial Use 
    and Derivative Revenue. This prohibition applies regardless of:
    (a) The amount of revenue generated;
    (b) Whether the revenue was intended;
    (c) Whether the revenue is related to the Software's primary function;
    (d) Whether the user is an individual, organization, or entity;
    (e) Any other circumstances.

