7. BREACH OF AGREEMENT AND REMEDIES
================================================================================

7.1 Any use of the Software that constitutes Commercial Use or generates 
    Derivative Revenue without a valid Commercial License Agreement constitutes:
    (a) A material breach of this Agreement;
    (b) Copyright infringement;
    (c) Unauthorized use of intellectual property;
    (d) A violation of applicable laws.

7.2 Upon any breach of this Agreement, Licensor may:
    (a) Immediately terminate this license and all rights granted hereunder;
    (b) Demand immediate cessation of all use of the Software;
    (c) Demand immediate deletion of all copies of the Software;
    (d) Pursue all available legal remedies, including but not limited to:
        - Injunctive relief to prevent further use;
        - Monetary damages;
        - Statutory damages for copyright infringement;
        - Punitive damages;
        - Attorney's fees and costs;
        - Any other relief available under applicable law.

7.3 MONETARY DAMAGES: In the event of any breach of this Agreement, Licensee 
    shall be liable to Licensor for:
    (a) ALL revenue, income, profit, or financial gain (including Derivative 
        Revenue) generated from or connected to the unauthorized use of the 
        Software, multiplied by a factor of three (3) as liquidated damages;
    (b) Statutory damages for copyright infringement, which may be up to 
        $150,000 per work infringed under U.S. copyright law, or equivalent 
        amounts under other applicable laws;
    (c) All costs and expenses incurred by Licensor in connection with 
        enforcing this Agreement, including but not limited to:
        - Attorney's fees;
        - Court costs;
        - Investigation costs;
        - Audit costs;
        - Expert witness fees;
        - Any other costs or expenses;
    (d) Interest on all amounts due at the rate of 18% per annum, or the 
        maximum rate allowed by applicable law, whichever is greater;
    (e) Any other damages available under applicable law.

7.4 LIQUIDATED DAMAGES: The parties agree that the damages set forth in 
    Section 7.3(a) are reasonable estimates of the actual damages that would 
    be difficult to calculate precisely, and constitute liquidated damages, 
    not penalties.

7.5 MULTIPLE VIOLATIONS: Each instance of unauthorized Commercial Use or 
    generation of Derivative Revenue constitutes a separate violation, and 
    damages shall be calculated separately for each violation.

7.6 CONTINUING VIOLATIONS: For continuing violations, damages shall be 
    calculated for each day the violation continues.

7.7 NO LIMITATION: The remedies set forth in this Section 7 are in addition 
    to, and not in lieu of, any other remedies available under applicable law.

